                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "35a9f7bb-e9df-450b-ba7a-9278efea53b1",
                        "entry_id": "e999d87f-084c-36b3-8a2b-4236cb06aca7",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "aberrated"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ca528b8-3a85-3955-a48a-0fb5066984cb",
                        "entry_id": "e999d87f-084c-36b3-8a2b-4236cb06aca7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To go astray; to diverge; to deviate (from); deviate from."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "50480c79-abc5-4694-8d54-e04b0573d965",
                                "sense_id": "2ca528b8-3a85-3955-a48a-0fb5066984cb",
                                "text": "1765, Peter Dollond, letter to James Short dated 7 February, 1765, in Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society, Volume 55, London, 1766, p. 55,\n[…] the surfaces of the concave lens may be so proportioned as to aberrate exactly equal to the convex lens, near the axis […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b82f7421-3559-470e-a3fb-67fee269e794",
                                "sense_id": "2ca528b8-3a85-3955-a48a-0fb5066984cb",
                                "text": "Such, indeed, were the primitive regulations of the greater number of monastic institutions; but the abominable and luxurious indulgences into which they afterwards aberrated, the page of history amply unfolds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2255d1fc-0d2b-4336-bfb4-cda7b3264f22",
                                "sense_id": "2ca528b8-3a85-3955-a48a-0fb5066984cb",
                                "text": "1839, Thomas De Quincey, “Lake Reminiscences: No. V, Southey, Wordsworth, and Coleridge” originally published in Tait’s Magazine, August 1839, in David Masson (editor), The Collected Writings of Thomas De Quincey, London: A. & C. Black, 1896, Volume 2, Chapter 5, pp. 340-341,\n[…] the barriers, which to them limit the view, and give to it, together with the contraction, all the distinctness and definite outline of limitation, are, in nine cases out of ten, the product of their own defective and aberrating vision, and not real barriers at all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6712bd5-3f04-4b33-9182-724f4724de1a",
                                "sense_id": "2ca528b8-3a85-3955-a48a-0fb5066984cb",
                                "text": "[…] after all the Governor of a Southern state has got to try to act like he regrets having to aberrate from being a gentleman—"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad5f3c03-0d7a-3ed6-ad3f-fd1ba53336cd",
                        "entry_id": "e999d87f-084c-36b3-8a2b-4236cb06aca7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To distort; to cause aberration of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2610535a-c408-4f29-96ae-cfe1e128c863",
                                "sense_id": "ad5f3c03-0d7a-3ed6-ad3f-fd1ba53336cd",
                                "text": "1893, Bret Harte, Sally Dows, Chapter 6, in Sally Dows and Other Stories, Boston: Houghton Mifflin, p. 104,\nHe saw them through no aberrating mist of tenderness or expediency—but with the single directness of the man of action."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f979ff89-9ad0-465e-bb9e-7e81ccfc0320",
                                "sense_id": "ad5f3c03-0d7a-3ed6-ad3f-fd1ba53336cd",
                                "text": "He and Phœbe had had a senseless quarrel […] and she had left. It was an aberrated fulfillment of her old jesting threat that if he did not behave himself she would leave him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1692f450-d236-4e9f-9922-401218030b69",
                                "sense_id": "ad5f3c03-0d7a-3ed6-ad3f-fd1ba53336cd",
                                "text": "Don’t imagine that there was any sudden and complete renunciation such as overcomes the luckless and often temporarily aberrated victim of a highly emotionalized revival meeting; this would have been, at best, but temporary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "382a04dd-774e-4aef-abc4-c3c7313f3238",
                                "sense_id": "ad5f3c03-0d7a-3ed6-ad3f-fd1ba53336cd",
                                "text": "1950, Louis S. London, Sexual Deviations, cited in reviews in Time, 17 April, 1950 (“Medicine: The Abnormal”) and Journal of the Indiana State Medical Association, Volume 43, August, 1950, p. 802,\n[…] sexually aberrated individuals can be treated most successfully via the method of psycho-analytic psychotherapy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3651acd-b86f-4380-aa32-7ce3c8680a64",
                                "sense_id": "ad5f3c03-0d7a-3ed6-ad3f-fd1ba53336cd",
                                "text": "As these monographs and as these occasional exhibition catalogues on some handful of Canadian Impressionists started to appear, once again, I was surprised (to say it with the utmost respect) that they were aberrated, there was no timeline, there was no continuity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3fc9edc-ddd1-49da-94d5-1a3677ecdab4",
                        "source_entry_id": "e999d87f-084c-36b3-8a2b-4236cb06aca7",
                        "source_sense_description": "to deviate from; to go astray",
                        "target_lang_word": "aberrer",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aberrer",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59d05450-edd6-3f9b-9240-33cae4b3c664",
                                        "entry_id": "e4e23456-0c2b-3f74-b5a7-48c2604b6f6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "s'écarter du chemin, dévier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a44b00e-8455-3ac0-b997-0870b4bc9176",
                                        "entry_id": "e4e23456-0c2b-3f74-b5a7-48c2604b6f6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Être dans l’erreur, dans le faux ; se tromper ; s’écarter du bon sens ou de la norme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6e9a2e8-1dd9-4da9-b975-5c7b9c7b7926",
                                                "sense_id": "8a44b00e-8455-3ac0-b997-0870b4bc9176",
                                                "text": "Durant sa dernière maladie, son esprit aberrait la plupart du temps, et dans ses moments de raison, il pleurait sur la vie délicieuse qui allait lui échapper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f099f30-8ded-4e7a-88f5-3c4e7b416060",
                                                "sense_id": "8a44b00e-8455-3ac0-b997-0870b4bc9176",
                                                "text": "Comme la plupart des mystiques, et des mystiques libres qui vagabondent sur le terrain sans assiette de l’examen individuel, la femme des Horizons célestes peut aberrer ou aller trop loin dans la lettre même de son ouvrage, mais elle doit être pardonnée pour la pureté de ses motifs et la beauté de ses affections."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd89b795-a360-44ae-aaef-1980d54da4e8",
                                                "sense_id": "8a44b00e-8455-3ac0-b997-0870b4bc9176",
                                                "text": "Certes, je pouvais aberrer, comme on dit, je crois, en astronomie. Mais j’étais curieux de savoir si je tomberais juste, en partant d’une demi-certitude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e71ed5ce-6b0b-470a-90d9-fdf0138a8335",
                                                "sense_id": "8a44b00e-8455-3ac0-b997-0870b4bc9176",
                                                "text": "Vous aberrez, mes compères. Il convient de punir ces mauvais augures... Que les porteurs de fausses nouvelles me soient amenés et qu’on leur coupe les oreilles..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
